-- §5  Which buffers the corpus sizes, and which of them read zero.
# One row per (buffer, evidence) from the slack census over every filing: sized, sized at zero,
# blank, and the total.
#
# Sized zero against unmeasured
#   A sized zero and an unmeasured buffer are opposite claims, and this splits them. Many corpus
#   layers that size their capacity slack size it at zero, a filer saying the supply cannot
#   stretch. That is the tightest possible bound, not a missing one.
#
# Prose about this number goes stale
#   It is wrong as soon as the corpus moves, and the corpus moves. A sentence that states it is
#   read by no program, so the number is printed here instead.
-- reports/slack_census.sqlc over every filing, projected for the example.
SELECT c.buffer         AS "buffer!",
       c.evidence       AS "evidence",
       c.sized          AS "sized!",
       c.sized_at_zero  AS "sized_at_zero!",
       c.absent         AS "absent!",
       c.rows           AS "rows!"
FROM (
    :compose(reports/slack_census.sqlc, @scope = scope/every_filing.sqlc)
) c
ORDER BY c.buffer, c.evidence
